  "id": "adjektivdeklination",
  "name": "Adjective position: une voiture bleue, un grand homme",
  "level": "B1",
  "variety": "fr-FR",
  "subtitle": "Most French adjectives come after the noun: une voiture bleue, un collègue français. A few short, common ones come before: un petit appartement, une bonne idée. Some change their meaning with the position: un grand homme is a great man, un homme grand is a tall man.",
  "briefMarks": ["une voiture bleue", "un petit appartement", "un bel arbre", "un nouvel ami", "de bons amis", "un grand homme", "un homme grand", "ma propre voiture"],
  "source": "icanspeak French original text (grammar-b1 run, 2026-11-08)",
  "concept": {
    "comic": {
      "title": "Un {grand} homme ou un homme {grand} ?",
      "panels": [
        {
          "caption": "Before the noun",
          "tag": "{grand} = great",
          "left": { "name": "regi", "expr": "thinking", "say": "Comment est ton médecin ?" },
          "right": { "name": "bruno", "expr": "happy", "say": "C'est un {grand} homme. Il aide tout le monde." }
        },
        {
          "caption": "After the noun",
          "tag": "{grand} = tall",
          "left": { "name": "quaki", "expr": "oops", "say": "Regarde cet homme {grand} !" },
          "right": { "name": "hamsti", "expr": "happy", "say": "Oui, il fait deux mètres !" }
        }
      ]
    },
    "flow": [
      { "text": "un / une + nom + adjectif", "variant": "verb" },
      { "text": "beau · bon · grand · petit · jeune · vieux · nouveau · joli · mauvais · gros", "variant": "prep" },
      { "text": "un grand homme ≠ un homme grand" }
    ],
    "exampleHtml": "Sofia a une <span class=\"vp-verb\">petite</span> voiture <span class=\"vp-verb\">bleue</span>. · Léa habite dans un <span class=\"vp-verb\">bel</span> appartement. · Nous avons de <span class=\"vp-verb\">bons</span> voisins. · Mon <span class=\"vp-verb\">ancien</span> chef est un homme <span class=\"vp-verb\">grand</span> et mince.",
    "qa": [
      {
        "html": "The normal place is <strong>after the noun</strong>: colours, nationalities, shapes, and most longer adjectives. <em>une voiture bleue, un collègue algérien, une table ronde, un homme fatigué, une idée intéressante.</em>",
        "tag": "After the noun"
      },
      {
        "html": "A group of short, common adjectives comes <strong>before the noun</strong>: <em>beau, bon, grand, petit, jeune, vieux, nouveau, joli, mauvais, gros</em> (and also <em>premier, dernier, long</em>). <em>un petit appartement, une bonne idée, un gros problème, une jolie rue.</em>",
        "tag": "Before the noun"
      },
      {
        "html": "Two adjectives: each goes to its own place. <em>une petite voiture bleue, un beau manteau vert, une grande maison blanche.</em> Two adjectives from the short group stay together before the noun: <em>un joli petit village.</em>",
        "tag": "Two adjectives"
      },
      {
        "html": "Before a masculine noun that starts with a vowel or a silent <em>h</em>, three adjectives have a special form: <strong>bel, nouvel, vieil</strong>. <em>un bel arbre, un nouvel appartement, un vieil homme, un bel hôtel.</em> With a consonant: <em>un beau jardin, un nouveau voisin, un vieux livre.</em>",
        "tag": "bel · nouvel · vieil"
      },
      {
        "html": "Before a plural adjective, <strong>des</strong> becomes <strong>de</strong> (written standard): <em>de bons amis, de grandes fenêtres, de beaux enfants.</em> Singular and adjective after the noun do not change: <em>un bon ami, des amis fidèles.</em> In speech you will also hear <em>des bons amis</em>.",
        "tag": "des → de"
      },
      {
        "html": "The position can <strong>change the meaning</strong>. Before the noun the meaning is often figurative, after it literal: <em>un grand homme</em> (a great man) / <em>un homme grand</em> (a tall man); <em>mon ancien appartement</em> (my former flat) / <em>un immeuble ancien</em> (an old building); <em>ma propre voiture</em> (my own car) / <em>une voiture propre</em> (a clean car).",
        "tag": "Meaning and position"
      },
      {
        "html": "More pairs: <em>un cher ami</em> (a dear friend) / <em>un hôtel cher</em> (an expensive hotel); <em>le dernier jour</em> (the last day of a series) / <em>la semaine dernière</em> (last week, the one just gone).",
        "tag": "More pairs"
      }
    ],
    "noteHtml": "Common mistakes: ✗ <em>une voiture rouge petite</em> → ✓ <em>une petite voiture rouge</em>. ✗ <em>un nouveau appartement</em> → ✓ <em>un nouvel appartement</em>. ✗ <em>des bons amis</em> in a written text → ✓ <em>de bons amis</em>. ✗ <em>un américain collègue</em> → ✓ <em>un collègue américain</em>. Agreement is the same as always, see <a href=\"/accord-des-adjectifs\">adjective agreement</a> and <a href=\"/pluriels\">plurals</a>.",
    "reference": {
